DevOps Scenario Series

Topic: TLS Certificates

Scenario:
You’re working as a DevOps Engineer.
One day, a teammate says:
"Bro, the app isn’t opening. Chrome is shouting ‘Your connection is not private’."

You check… and yes, it’s a TLS/SSL certificate issue.


Possible reasons:
Certificate has expired.
Domain name doesn’t match the cert.
A self-signed cert is being used in prod.
Intermediate/chain cert is missing.


Solution:
Check expiry date → Renew the cert if it’s expired.
Verify domain mapping → Make sure the CN/SAN in the cert matches your site.
Use CA-signed cert → Replace self-signed with a trusted CA certificate.
Fix chain → Add missing intermediate certs in the server config.
Prevent future issues → Automate renewals with Let’s Encrypt, Certbot, or Cloud provider cert managers.


 Freshers Tip:
 When TLS/SSL breaks, don’t panic. 90% of the time it’s expiry, mismatch, or missing chain. Start with these checks first
